; Logical Truncating Cast : the EXPLICIT lossy float -> integer
; conversion (torch.int()/long()). Truncation toward zero is the ruled
; semantics; PyTorch declares NaN/inf/out-of-range as undefined, so the
; runtime refuses those loudly. The TARGET dtype rides in the term; the
; bit width changes, so this is always a materializer, never a view.
; Plain LogicalCast stays lossless-only.
(constructor LogicalTruncCast (LogicalTensor Dtype) LogicalTensor)
